[26.131314, "o", "change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n   199\t\r\n   200\t## Email Excerpts (archived thread)\r\n   201\t\r\n   202\tNon-authoritative mailbox export kept for chronology; do not merge these rows.\r\n   203\t\r\n   204\tFrom: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   205\tSubject: Re: TXN-88519dfd-79ff-5de0-ae59-862ab932bc25\r\n   206\tsent: 2020-01-01\r\n   207\tstatus: reversed\r\n   208\t\r\n   209\tFrom: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   210\tSubject: Re: TXN-51cc9d8a-ea13-56ab-af16-c55e1716132f\r\n   211\tsent: 2024-01-01\r\n   212\tstatus: approved\r\n   213\t\r\n   214\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n   215\t\r\n   216\tInterview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n   217\tamendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n   218\toutput). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n   219\trejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n   220\tcontains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other sende"]
[26.131364, "o", "rs.\r\n   221\t\r\n   222\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence — supporting chronology\r\n   223\t\r\n   224\tRegional lead E. Novak hosted a readout on capital project capitalization where finance controllers disputed whether unsigned meeting notes should override ledger owners; investigators cited Brief 05 during the session.\r\n   225\t\r\n   226\tSite visit #525 to fixed assets exported 19 compliance threads tied to capital project capitalization. Reviewers noted that owner field churn appeared whenever correction batches straddled a weekend wire cutoff.\r\n   227\t\r\n   228\tGrant compliance WP-9559 tied capital project capitalization attestation gaps to ledger slice confusion visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.\r\n   229\t\r\n   230\tPeer review #804 of fixed assets sampling found 19 mislinked emails on capital project capitalization. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sender restrictions.\r\n   231\t\r\n   232\tCommittee "]
